    "head_commit_message": "feat(sim): the 2D feel test reads the worker's snapshots (spec 39 step 10d-ii)\n\nFieldState now plays the field on the worker, through FieldPlayer\n(field_play/player.rs), and every read shows the newest snapshot. Each\nframe owes the clock's ticks and takes what was played, never waiting.\nOrders and a replay's commands queue for the next boundary between\nticks, so records and replays are unchanged. Units hold at the newest\ntick while the next isn't ready (Worker::reached), and the HUD says\nSIMULATION BEHIND when time is dropped. run_ticks also waits for every\norder given before it, for tests and headless play.\n\nRefs #557. Cascade #727.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi3CLK7z2mXK2PcNuCi",
